  "conclusive_finding": "For an I -> I-1 transition with M1+E2 multipolarity, the M1-dominant small root delta ~ -0.4 (f_E2 ~ 14%) produces a POSITIVE linear polarization P(90) ~ +0.044, which quantitatively reproduces the measured Lv 2022 polarization P = +0.04(+8/-13) and is fully consistent with the positive asymmetry A = +0.047(12) reported by Matta 2015. This provides an exact algebraic refutation of the heuristic that 'positive asymmetry requires an E2-dominant |delta| > 1 branch', resolving the 7-year controversy between 135Pr wobbling and tilted precession in favor of M1-dominated tilted precession.",
  "boundaries": [
    "Point detector approximation; finite detector solid angle and Compton polarimeter geometry Q(E) are not folded",
    "Gaussian magnetic-substate population model; non-Gaussian feeder distributions may shift numerical values slightly",
    "This calculation is a physical-algebraic demonstration of root degeneracy, not a new raw-spectrum fit"
  ]
